      "text": "This agent is registered with SohoPay, but it can't pay merchants yet. The credit evaluation is still open, and only you can complete it.\n\n`get_context` showed that most steps were already done, so I didn't repeat them. The only action I took this session was requesting a fresh borrower token.\n\n| Item | State |\n|---|---|\n| Borrower ID | `89a20b20-67ad-46b8-8fff-abd9e390ae41` |\n| Operational agent / terminal | `oa_ec3484ae0c4e588a` / `term_0f26a5a4f0876f52` |\n| Wallet proof | Verified (`0xb79a…9913`) |\n| Workload key | Registered (jkt `0Yof4xzH…tJ4s`) |\n| Agent grant | ACTIVE |\n| Handle | `@agentbbc723` claimed |\n| Borrower token | Issued with all 6 scopes and no dropped scopes. It expires in 900 seconds (15 minutes). |\n\n**What's left:** `EVALUATE_CREDIT` is a browser step for you as the borrower. The credit eligibility status is `NOT_EVALUATED`, and `get_context` reports `can_pay: false` and `spend_ready: false`. The response gave no URL for it. Running `get_context` again should show the link, or you can start the evaluation from your SohoPay account. Once it's done, I can re-check with `get_context`. If a credit offer then needs review, that is also a step for you in the browser.\n\nI didn't do step 7, the `POST /api/v1/auth/authorization-context` call. It's an HTTP endpoint, and no SohoPay tool in this session exposes it."
